        "raw": "<p>I&#39;m not going to say that my players are awful at diplomacy, but when presented with the option of either making peace with someone who is punching them or continuing to punch back until that person is defeated, they tend to pick the second option.</p><p>That said, in Prime Wardens #86, if Haka gets impatient and starts beating the stuffing out of them and their new friend Tempest, in all likelihood, they aren&#39;t going to continue to try and talk her down. This is... problematic, because the pdf doesn&#39;t tell me how to run Haka if she&#39;s a threat. What dice do I roll? How many hits can she take? Do I just make her a D12 Lieutenant?</p><p>Basically, what should I do if my players want to straight up fight Haka?</p>",
