        "raw": "<p>I&#39;d have a hard time justifying &quot;the heroes cannot win this fight.&quot;&nbsp; She&#39;s tough, but standing up the the whole Freedom Five+Unity at once?&nbsp; I don&#39;t think so.&nbsp; Especially since we&#39;ll have full stats for her when the full game comes out.</p><p>I&#39;m thinking what I&#39;d do is make her a &quot;phantom&quot; full villain with &quot;real&quot; HP.&nbsp; Except that she just soaks the damage, takes out Tempest at the earliest opportunity, and then the next scene begins with her still hostile.&nbsp; If the heroes attempt to defend her at any sort of risk to themselves, that counts as her &quot;convince her to listen&quot; the first time and then &quot;convince her the heroes aren&#39;t villains&quot; the second time.&nbsp; If, after the battle, the heroes still persist in attacking her, she tries to flee.&nbsp; If the heroes pursue her... well, only Legacy and Tachyon have a chance of doing so, and that fight she can win, especially when they&#39;re weakened by the spirit battle.</p>",
